From 0560e47c906210697dac6dcea6e865adfb72bc62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daily-max <daily-max@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:25:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: pause button, 3-2-1 resume countdown, exit to title
 screen

- On-screen pause button in the top-right corner: pause glyph while
  flying, play glyph while paused, hidden in the menu and on game over.
  It paints above the overlay so it doubles as a Resume control, and
  pointer tracking skips it so tapping pause never moves the ship.
- Resuming now runs a 3-2-1 countdown in a new `resuming` mode. The
  world stays frozen for all of it, held directions are remembered and
  apply the moment it hits zero, and P/Esc/the corner button cancel it
  back to the paused panel. Runs on the fixed 120 Hz step, so a stalled
  frame cannot skip or stretch it.
- The paused panel gains Exit, which banks the best score and returns to
  the title screen.
- fix: one-shot keys ignore keyboard autorepeat. Holding P or Esc for
  longer than a tap used to toggle pause many times and leave the game
  resumed with the panel still up.
- fix: Space/Enter on a focused button is no longer swallowed by the
  global key handler, so Tab then Enter now works on Start, Resume, Exit
  and the corner pause button.
- Rebase the fixed-step clock on resume, so a paused interval is never
  paid back as a burst of catch-up steps on the first frame back.
